@baseUrl = http://localhost:8092
@accountId = ACC-001

### 1. Open account -> stream version 0
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "accountId": "{{accountId}}",
  "ownerName": "Hristo",
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### 2. Deposit -> stream version 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 150.00,
  "reference": "salary"
}

### 3. Withdraw -> stream version 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/withdrawals
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 20.00,
  "reference": "groceries"
}

### 4. Current state is rebuilt from all events -> balance 130.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/state

### 5. Historical state at stream version 1 -> balance 150.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/state/1

### 6. Inspect immutable history.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/history

### 7. Read projection does not exist until events are projected.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/projection

### 8. Catch projection up.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/projections/all

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/projection

### 9. Create snapshot at current version.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/snapshot

### 10. New event after snapshot.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/deposits
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "amount": 70.00,
  "reference": "bonus"
}

### 11. Snapshot load replays only the tail event.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/accounts/{{accountId}}/state?useSnapshot=true

### 12. Projection can be rebuilt entirely from source events.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/event-sourcing/projections/rebuild
